    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d73">

                <pb facs="0154" n="74" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg74"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15a3/774: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Castle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-03-23T12:00:00+09:00">March 23,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received March 23—4:33 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>55. Your 55, March 21, 5 p.m.<anchor n="91a" xml:id="d73-f1"/> Repeat to
                        London.<anchor n="92" xml:id="d73-f2"/></p>
                <p>Wakatsuki gave out a statement that this is not an American proposal but an
                    agreement which was reached by three delegations. His statement was published in
                    all the Japanese newspapers yesterday morning.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
